"Fix finding B5 (U1 review R-09): db:worker has no equivalent of the local-only guard that db:seed and db:reset have. Today scripts/db/worker.ts setupWorker calls loadToolingSettings (which only runs assertLocalAddress on DATABASE_URL and SUPABASE_URL) and then connects and runs `drop schema if exists \"worker_N\" cascade` (with --reset), creates and migrates the worker schema, truncates its tables and deletes auth.users rows by worker email prefix. A hosted database reached through a loopback tunnel would pass the address check and be changed. Fix: reuse the existing guard in scripts/db/local-guard.ts. (1) Before connecting, run assertLocalSettings (address check plus the default-local-password check, assertLocalStackPassword) on the settings. (2) After connecting, run assertLocalStack (the identity check) and close the client when it refuses, as connectLocalStack does; the cleanest shape is to use connectLocalStack(settings, deps.connect) in setupWorker. IMPORTANT: db:worker is itself one of the tools that creates the migration tracking table (the runner does `create table if not exists ...applied_migrations`, and db:start does not migrate), so the identity check must NOT require that the tracking table already exists for the worker: give assertLocalStack/connectLocalStack an optional parameter (for example { requireManaged: false }, default true so seed and reset keep their exact behaviour) and have the worker pass false; the other identity reasons (postgres database, supabase_admin role, JWT secret hash when present) stay required. Keep the worker error wrapping (ToolingError step names, worker/schema detail) working: a refusal should surface as a ToolingError with step guard and the worker and schema in its detail, and must not echo any password. Existing tests: scripts/db/tooling.test.ts uses FAKE_URL with the password fake-db-password in the worker tests and a fakeSql that does not answer the identity query: update the worker tests so they use a loopback URL with the Supabase CLI default password (the one in LOCAL.databaseUrl of scripts/db/local-guard.test.ts, postgres:postgres) and a fake that answers the identity query like local-guard.test.ts does; keep other tooling tests (migrate) unchanged. tests/database/stack-support.ts and the real-stack tests call setupWorker against the real local stack with the default password and must keep working. New tests: setupWorker refuses a non-default password before any connection is made, refuses a database that does not identify itself as the local stack (client closed, no drop/create/truncate/delete statement run), and still works on a stack whose tracking table does not exist yet. Also mention in the README db:worker description that it refuses anything but the local stack, like seed and reset. Record in aidlc/spaces/default/intents/261012-real-backend-local/follow-ups/minor-findings-plan.md under B5 that db:worker now has the guard, and note that db:migrate (scripts/db/migrate.ts) has only the address check, which is out of scope here and listed as a separate possible follow-up. Source: plan group B5 of that file. Skip Reverse Engineering and the deployment stages (the person already decided that for these fixes)."
